
To install it, after downloading it, before opening the .dmg file, run in an /Applications/Terminal.app

xattr -d com.apple.quarantine /path/to/your/dmg/file.dmg

Then open the .dmg file and drag the @mrv2_NAME@ icon to the 
Applications directory.  If there's already an existant @mrv2_NAME@ version, we
recommend you overwrite it (in case it does not work well for you, you can 
always revert to a previous version).

As the @mrv2_NAME@ application is currently neither code signed nor notarized, 
you need to do another fearful step.

You need to double click on the installation.command file.  On macOS 15+ and later, you may have to force Mac OS (in the Security part of the System Settings) to allow the file to run.

You will be asked for your password once and the codesigning commands will be
run and then you will be able to enjoy @mrv2_NAME@.

